Subject: [PATCH] ssdk: disable NAT as well as NAPT at DESS initialization

The native Flow owner requires an unclaimed translation engine. Live DESS
reads show NAT enabled after initialization, which previously cleared only
the NAPT bit despite intending to disable both. Clear both enable bits so
the Flow owner can claim, program and subsequently enable translation.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/src/init/ssdk_init.c
+++ b/src/init/ssdk_init.c
@@ -3043,7 +3043,8 @@
 	/*set normal hash and disable nat/napt*/
 	qca_switch_reg_read(dev_id, 0x0e38, (a_uint8_t *)&reg_value, 4);
 	reg_value = (reg_value|0x1000000|0x8);
-	reg_value &= ~2;
+	/* Leave both translation engines disabled for the native Flow owner. */
+	reg_value &= ~3U;
 	qca_switch_reg_write(dev_id, 0x0e38, (a_uint8_t *)&reg_value, 4);
 	#ifdef IN_IP
 	fal_ip_vrf_base_addr_set(dev_id, 0, 0);
